=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_a3f7 — Both drive on weekdays; dinner at the dining table; sink is the kitchen work surface (fork of p_4e91)

The key change from p_4e91: the main evening meal is at dining_table_d1, not kitchen_table_k1. Day-0 evidence (Tuesday 20:00) shows plate_yuki, glass_yuki, and water_bottle_yuki all at dining_table_d1 while resident_1 (Yuki) is in the dining room. The kitchen_table_k1 serves breakfast and Omar's midday meal, but the family dinner table is the dining table.

A second change: cooking implements (pan, knife, cutting board, spatula) rest at sink_k1, not at counter_k1, cupboard_k1, or drawer_k_k1. The same day-0 look at 20:00 found pan, knife, cutting board, and spatula all at sink_k1, consistent with a post-cooking wash-up. The pot rests at pantry_shelf_k1. After dinner, glasses and the snack bowl also go to sink_k1 for washing (glass_yuki was at sink_k1 at 22:00).

Minor corrections: towel_yuki rests at bathroom_shelf_ba1 (evidence at 20:00), and plant_pot_2_shared is at counter_k1 (evidence at 20:00). Everything else from p_4e91 is retained: both drive on weekdays, weekend cycling 10:00–13:00, Yuki's work tools out 8:00–17:30, Omar's tablet at chair_k1.

What sets this apart from p_4e91: dinner items at dining_table_d1 (not kitchen_table_k1), cooking implements at sink_k1 (not counter/cupboard/drawer), pot at pantry_shelf_k1. What would refute it: plate_yuki or glass_yuki at kitchen_table_k1 during 19:00–20:00 on a weekday, or pan_shared at cupboard_k1 at 20:00.

